  "deviations": [
    "The page now has the timeline navigator the canvas predates: a time window (whole record, instruction period, chosen dates), a way of reading (chronology, activity, overview map) and a scale. The harness opens the overview map and the instruction period; the controls share rows, but the board starts lower than on the canvas, so the boxes below them are probed for size, colour and type, not for their vertical place (rect.y allowed on those probes).",
    "Text under 17px is raised to 17px; dot words (14px on the canvas) are 17px, so the harness renders the artboard the same way.",
    "The canvas 'Question 2 only' chip is not built: it is a shortcut filter the API and the brief do not describe.",
    "The middle 'Feb to Oct 2024' segment shows the case's period in question and asks the server for those days; the canvas draws it as the highlighted choice and the harness clicks it.",
    "Lane subtitles read '4 entries' (count only); the canvas has a words-per-lane summary the API does not carry.",
    "The chosen dot with a halo (15 May on the canvas) has no data behind it, so every checked dot is the plain size.",
    "Words under a dot are placed above or below by a width estimate (neighbours take turns); the canvas places them by hand.",
    "Tap areas: segments, chips and the switch keep 52px through ::after hit boxes while drawn at canvas size.",
    "Lanes with more than four entries, or dots too close for words, show dots only and fold their entries into a 'See all n in date order' list (the navigator's behaviour); the canvas draws every dot with words, so lane rows are taller and 'row 1' is not compared by height.",
    "The first line under the title is the navigator's own: 'Open any entry to see how it looked on the day', plus the blind-read hint; the canvas reads 'Click any dot to open its page', so the title block is wider (rect.w allowed on h1 and intro).",
